RESULT: Every function in the module declares ConfirmImpact="high", including the three
actually called during delegation (Set-ADSyncBasicReadPermissions, ~line 84 or 241 area;
Set-ADSyncMsDsConsistencyGuidPermissions; Set-ADSyncPasswordHashSyncPermissions, the one whose
per-domain loop stalled, at or near line 1832 — matching the ~1863 line the report's original
diagnosis cited from reading the file directly). This confirms the report's ShouldProcess stall
diagnosis was correct, not merely plausible: with PowerShell's default $ConfirmPreference of
"High", these specific cmdlets would trigger an interactive confirmation prompt, which a
scheduled task with no attached console cannot answer — matching the observed symptom exactly.
No correction needed to the report's Phase 3 paragraph.
